From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile <noreply@domicile.invalid>
Date: Sun, 7 Sep 2026 11:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: open the producer's socket at startup

A desktop cannot boot without this.

The broker's socket was opened on first use, and first use was a page
calling canvas.embedExternalSurface(). That is right for every spike page,
which embeds as it loads. It is wrong for a shell, which mounts an <app>
element when the host announces a window, learns of windows from the
compositor, and reaches the compositor -- the producer -- over this socket.
So the socket waited for an embed, the embed waited for a window, and the
window waited for the socket.

spike-shell.sh found it by being the first thing to drive a real shell
rather than a page written for the guard.

Here rather than anywhere earlier: GetHostFrameSinkManager() reads through
ImageTransportFactory, which is set two lines above, and binding the socket
is a mkdir and a bind that PostCreateThreads is allowed to post off-thread.
---
 content/browser/browser_main_loop.cc | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/content/browser/browser_main_loop.cc b/content/browser/browser_main_loop.cc
--- a/content/browser/browser_main_loop.cc
+++ b/content/browser/browser_main_loop.cc
@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@
 #include "content/browser/browser_thread_impl.h"
 #include "content/browser/compositor/viz_process_transport_factory.h"
 #include "content/browser/cpu_performance/cpu_performance.h"
+#include "content/browser/domicile/domicile_frame_sink_broker.h"
 #include "content/browser/download/save_file_manager.h"
 #include "content/browser/field_trial_synchronizer.h"
 #include "content/browser/first_party_sets/first_party_set_parser.h"
@@ -1427,6 +1428,14 @@ void BrowserMainLoop::PostCreateThreadsImpl() {
       compositing_mode_reporter_impl_.get());
   transport_factory->ConnectHostFrameSinkManager();
   ImageTransportFactory::SetFactory(std::move(transport_factory));
+
+  // Domicile's producer socket, if this browser was given a path for one. It
+  // has to be open before any page embeds, because in a shell the page cannot
+  // embed until a window exists and no window can exist until the compositor
+  // has connected over it. Nothing happens without
+  // --domicile-broker-socket. See
+  // content/browser/domicile/domicile_frame_sink_broker.h.
+  StartDomicileFrameSinkBroker();
 
 #if defined(USE_AURA)
   env_->set_context_factory(GetContextFactory());
